  "fashion": {
    "Overview": "A custom-decorated battle jacket, which is a central element of Punk fashion, representing the DIY ethos through hand-painted slogans, patches, and studs. Designer Vivienne Westwood in her infamous \"DESTROY\" T-shirt (c. 1977), which features a swastika and an inverted crucifix. The design is a primary example of the punk movement's use of fascist iconography for anti-establishment shock value."
